","Climate change can affect the prevalence and transmission of parasitic infections in various ecosystems and host communities through several mechanisms. These factors include changes in temperature, precipitation, and the availability of habitats for both the parasite and its host species. Some of the ways in which climate change can affect the prevalence and transmission of parasitic infections include:

