","Saltional conduction is a process by which electrical signals travel through nerve fibers (nerocytes) at an increased rate compared to non-saltatory conduction. The primary difference lies in the presence of myelin, a fatty tissue layer that surrounds nerve fibers in myelated nerve fibers.

