   \[
   \text{Weight of remaining gas} = 250 \text{ g} - 57.5 \text{ g} + 57.6 \text{ g} = 250.1 \text{ g}
   \]

**Final Answers:**
- The amount of sulphur (S) that should be burnt in air to remove oxygen as SO₂ is \(\boxed{28.8 \text{ g}}\).
