","To determine the geometric mean of the soil-topolished rice transfer factor (TF) of \(^{147}\text{Cs}\), we would need the specific data for the transfer factors from multiple studies or studies at different locations. The geometric mean is calculated as the \(n\)th root of the product of the \(n\) values. Mathematically, if the transfer factors are \(TF_1, TF_2, TF_3, \ldots, TF_n\), the geometric mean is:

\[
\text{Geometric Mean} = \left( \prod_{i=1}^n TF_i \right)^{1/n} = \left( TF_1 \times TF_2 \times TF_3 \times \ldots \times TF_n \right)^{1/n}
\]

However, since you have provided the symbol \(^{147}\text{Cs}\), but the question asks for \(^{137}\text{Cs}\), I will assume the question intended to refer to \(^{137}\text{Cs}\).

