The two glycol groups react with the two carboxylate groups of salicylic acid to form a diesster. The structure is:

\[
\text{HOOC-C₆H₃-CH₃\text{OH}} \xrightarrow{\text{Glycol}} \text{HOOC-C₆H₃-CH₂\text{O}CH₂\text{O}}
