\[
[H_3O^+][OH^-] = K_w = 10^{-14} \text{ M}^2
\]
Given \([H_3O^+] = 10^{-4}\) M, we can find \([OH^-]\):
\[
[OH^-] = \frac{10^{-14}}{10^{-4}} = 10^{-10} \text{ M}
\]
Since \([H_3O^+] = 10^{-4}\) M and \([OH^-] = 10^{-10}\) M, the concentration of \([H_3O^+]\) is greater than \([OH^-]\). Therefore, the solution is acidic.

In general, the pH of the solution is:
\[
\text{pH} = -\log[H_3O^+] = -\log(10^{-4}) = 4
\]
