   - For 20°C seawater:
     - \( \rho = 1000 \, \text{kg/m}^3 \)
     - \( \mu = 0.001 \, \text{Pa·s} \)
     - \( \nu = \frac{\mu}{\rho} = 10^{-6} \, \text{m}^2/\text{s} \)
     - The effective diameter \( L \) is approximately the diameter of the fibers: \( L = 1 \times 10^{-3} \, \text{m} \).
   - \( Re_f = \frac{1000 \times 10^{-6} \times 10^{-3}}{0.001} = 10^{-3} \).
   - For \( Re_f \ll 1 \), the drag coefficient for the fibers is \( C_f \approx 12 \times \frac{\rho \mu^2}{L^2} \).
   - The drag coefficient for the porous plate is \( C_d \approx 0.0001 \times Re^2 \), where \( Re = \frac{\rho u L}{mu} \).

