\[
\Delta S_{\text{gas}} = \frac{Q_{\text{gas}}}{\Delta T_{\text{gas}}} \ln \left( \frac{T_{\text{cold}}}{T_{\text{hot}}} \right)
\]
The heat lost by the gas is:
\[
Q_{\text{gas}} = m_{\text{gas}} c_{\text{gas}} \Delta T_{\text{gas}}
\]
The heat transferred to the water is:
\[
Q_{\text{water}} = m_{\text{water}} L_{\text{water}}
\]
Since all the heat transferred from the gases goes to the water, the heat lost by the gas equals the heat gained by the water:
\[
m_{\text{gas}} c_{\text{gas}} \Delta T_{\text{gas}} = m_{\text{water}} L_{\text{water}}
\]
