The entropy production rate \( \Pi_S \) is given by:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{1}{T} \dot{Q}
\]
where \( \dot{Q} \) is the heat generated by the friction.

The heat generated by friction is given by:
\[
\dot{Q} = F_{\text{fr}} v
\]
Substituting this into the entropy production rate equation:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{1}{T} F_{\text{fr}} v
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\boxed{\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}}
\]
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

