\]
Given \( e = \frac{1}{3} \), the ratio of the velocity of the block after the collision to the velocity of the block before the collision is \( \frac{1}{3} \). 

The kinetic energy of the ball before the collision is:
\[
K_{\text{initial}} = \frac{1}{2} m v^2
\]
The kinetic energy of the ball after the collision is:
\[
K_{\text{final}} = \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{out}}^2
\]
Since \( e = \frac{v_{\text{out}}}{v_{\text{in}}} \), we have \( v_{\text{out}} = e v_{\text{in}} = \frac{1}{3} v \). Substituting this into the kinetic energy after the collision:
\[
K_{\text{final}} = \frac{1}{2} m \left( \frac{1}{3} v \right)^2 = \frac{1}{2} m \cdot \frac{1}{9} v^2 = \frac{1}{9} \left( \frac{1}{2} m v^2 \right) = \frac{1}{9} K_{\text{initial}}
\]
