(i) **Temperature after 5 minutes**:  
The lumped parameter model is applicable since the Biot number \( Bi = \frac{hL}{k} \) is much less than 0.1. The characteristic length \( L \) is calculated as:  
\[
L = \frac{\text{Volume}}{\text{Surface Area}} = \frac{\text{mass}}{\text{density} \times \text{surface area}} = \frac{1.2}{7150 \times 0.075} = 2.24 \times 10^{-3} \, \text{m}
\]  
The temperature after time \( \tau \) is given by:  
\[
\frac{T - T_\infty}{T_0 - T_\infty} = \exp\left(-\frac{hA}{\rho cV} \tau\right) = \exp\left(-\frac{h}{\rho cL} \tau\right)
\]  
Substituting \( \tau = 300 \) seconds (5 minutes):  
\[
\frac{T - 20}{345 - 20} = \exp\left(-\frac{56.8}{7150 \times 385 \times 2.24 \times 10^{-3}} \times 300\right) = 0.063
\]  
\[
T = 20 + 0.063 \times 325 = 40.5^\circ \text{C}
\]  
**Final answer**: \(\boxed{40.5^\circ \text{C}}\)

(ii) **Time to reach 50°C**:  
Using the same equation:  
\[
\frac{50 - 20}{345 - 20} = \exp\left(-\frac{56.8}{7150 \times 385 \times 2.24 \times 10^{-3}} \tau\right)
\]  
Taking the natural logarithm:  
\[
\ln\left(\frac{30}{325}\right) = -\frac{56.8}{7150 \times 385 \times 2.24 \times 10^{-3}} \tau
\]  
Solving for \( \tau \):  
\[
\tau = 258.7 \, \text{seconds}
\]  
**Final answer**: \(\boxed{258.7 \, \text{seconds}}\)

(iii) **Time constant**:  
The time constant \( \tau_c \) is the time at which the temperature ratio equals \( 1/e \):  
\[
\tau_c = \frac{\rho c L}{h} = \frac{7150 \times 385 \times 2.24 \times 10^{-3}}{56.8} = 108.6 \, \text{seconds}
\]  
